# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
/aws-netpath

# Go
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.test
*.out
/vendor/

# Collected snapshots are models of a real network. They are excluded by policy,
# not by redaction: nothing in this tool attempts to sanitise a snapshot, so a
# snapshot must never be committed. Fixtures under testdata/ are hand-written
# and use documentation ranges only, so they stay tracked.
/snapshot.json
/snapshot-*.json
snapshot*.json

# The name patterns above only catch files called snapshot*.json, so
# `collect -output prod-net.json` still leaves a committable snapshot behind. A
# dedicated directory is harder to get wrong: write snapshots under snapshots/
# and the name no longer matters.
/snapshots/

!internal/query/testdata/*.json
!examples/*.json

# Kiro spec execution telemetry is machine-generated per-run state: execution
# ids, chat session ids, timestamps. It churns on every task run and conflicts
# meaninglessly on a shared branch, and tasks.md already records the outcome.
# The spec documents themselves — requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md,
# .config.kiro — stay tracked.
.kiro/specs/*/tasks.meta.json

# Terraform
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Credentials and local config
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
